            Theme 02 · Waves and upper-ocean mixing
          </p>

          <h2>
            Where can waves still influence mixing beneath
            Arctic sea ice?
          </h2>

          <p class="question">
            The result:
          </p>

          <p>
            Using coupled neXtSIM-WAVEWATCH III simulations from
            2018-2022, I led the first pan-Arctic assessment of
            Langmuir-turbulence mixing potential beneath sea ice.
          </p>

          <p>
            The marginal ice zone emerges as a distinct and highly
            intermittent forcing environment. Sea-ice concentration
            shapes the mean balance between wave- and shear-driven
            turbulence, but it does not uniquely determine local
            mixing potential; wave conditions and ice structure
            matter strongly.
          </p>

