            Theme 03 · A dynamic marginal ice zone
          </p>

          <h2>
            Why is the marginal ice zone more than a
            concentration threshold?
          </h2>

          <p class="question">
            The physical picture:
          </p>

          <p>
            The ice edge is not simply a line between open water and
            compact ice. It is a transition zone where wave forcing,
            wind forcing, fragmentation, and changing ice cover create
            repeated shifts between mixing regimes.
          </p>

          <p>
            This motivates my broader work: identify which
            satellite-observable properties of the ice and waves
            explain those transitions, and then use those observations
            to test how coupled models represent the ocean-ice interface.
          </p>

