          </p>

          <h2>
            When do ocean waves make satellite sea-ice
            concentration misleading?
          </h2>

          <p class="question">
            The current question:
          </p>

          <p>
            Passive-microwave sea-ice concentration products can
            disagree strongly in the marginal ice zone and during melt.
            I am investigating how wave and ice conditions affect these
            retrievals and which physical mechanisms explain the
            observed biases.
          </p>

          <p>
            The project combines complementary satellite observations
            with process understanding so that retrieval errors can be
            diagnosed by regime rather than treated as a single uniform
            uncertainty.
          </p>

